rl":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T12:45:01Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T12:45:01Z","body":"Just tested on `Godot v4.4.1.stable unknown - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Wed, 26 Mar 2025 07:48:57 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV RENOIR) - AMD Ryzen 7 4800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads)`\n\nCan not confirm the issue on my end. \n\n\nDoes it also happen when you disable the game embed window? Since this is new with Godot 4.4 iirc. \nAlso might be Wayland related (I am a bit confused by your info string stating both, Wayland and X11. But I am not super experienced with Linux Display Server stuff.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827489988/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827512836","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105688#issuecomment-2827512836","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105688","id":2827512836,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oiGwE","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T12:52:47Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T12:52:47Z","body":"This is likely a duplicate of #102580.\n\nI can't reproduce on Fedora 42 with KDE on Wayland, with the X11 display driver. But reports so far seemed to be about GNOME. Which DE are you using @BossyRomain?\n\n> (I am a bit confused by your info string stating both, Wayland and X11. But I am not super experienced with Linux Display Server stuff.)\n\nIt is indeed a bit confusing, but Godot's default driver driver is using X11, so when using it on Wayland, it's working via the XWayland compatibility layer. Godot also has a native Wayland display driver which can be opted into (which would likely also solve this lag issue for OP), but it doesn't support embedding the game window yet.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827512836/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827539703","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105688#issuecomment-2827539703","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105688","id":2827539703,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oiNT3","user":{"login":"Sch1nken","id":11414422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDE0NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11414422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken","html_url":"https://github.com/Sch1nken","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T12:59:37Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T12:59:37Z","body":"> It is indeed a bit confusing, but Godot's default driver driver is using X11, so when using it on Wayland, it's working via the XWayland compatibility layer. Godot also has a native Wayland display driver which can be opted into (which would likely also solve this lag issue for OP), but it doesn't support embedding the game window yet.\n\nThanks for the clarification. I knew about XWayland but was expecting to see it in the output string if used. But knowing that this means the same if also good.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827539703/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":nul